{"id":"expl:packages/memory/src/policy.ts@L117","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/memory/src/policy.ts","span":{"start":117,"end":117}},"file":"packages/memory/src/policy.ts","span":{"start":117,"end":117},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:0e48eed06bc4891ca3e52859336deeadc7682ce0ff5e3fa4b75d586e8948eaa1","meta":{"text":"Thrown when a policy document fails validation (unknown version, malformed profile, …)."}}
{"id":"expl:packages/memory/src/policy.ts@L127","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/memory/src/policy.ts","span":{"start":127,"end":127}},"file":"packages/memory/src/policy.ts","span":{"start":127,"end":127},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:506e93293f42a2ff4066007517396904a0bd69a2c4d4906bb32e5d6ed673d159","meta":{"text":"Validate a profile's shape (called by {@link assertValidPolicy}). Throws `PolicyError`."}}
{"id":"expl:packages/memory/src/policy.ts@L183","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/memory/src/policy.ts","span":{"start":183,"end":186}},"file":"packages/memory/src/policy.ts","span":{"start":183,"end":186},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:94021d9f2976d9d7d252781c2347c428f5aeb7a542ffa99ef335cb61146180df","meta":{"text":"Validate a parsed policy document. Unknown versions fail closed (PRD discipline: a future policy\nversion is not silently accepted). Throws `PolicyError` on any violation."}}
{"id":"expl:packages/memory/src/policy.ts@L223","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/memory/src/policy.ts","span":{"start":223,"end":226}},"file":"packages/memory/src/policy.ts","span":{"start":223,"end":226},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:4673b35fdc5a83c6dbe12659b5180c414afd1ea6c5a43b8e68a1952868658a59","meta":{"text":"Parse + validate a policy document from JSON text. Unknown versions + malformed profiles fail\nclosed with a `PolicyError` (never silently accepted)."}}
{"id":"expl:packages/memory/src/policy.ts@L238","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/memory/src/policy.ts","span":{"start":238,"end":242}},"file":"packages/memory/src/policy.ts","span":{"start":238,"end":242},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:a4b2b30c5b6aa2430e63b780c0bd11cdbae6dea82e944674bd7c25ef68fcf884","meta":{"text":"Load the committed policy from `<cribDir>/memory/policy.json`. Returns `undefined` when the file is\nabsent (no profiles configured — the gate cannot run; the CLI refuses evaluation). Throws\n`PolicyError` on a corrupt/malformed file (never silently returns a partial policy)."}}
{"id":"expl:packages/memory/src/policy.ts@L249","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/memory/src/policy.ts","span":{"start":249,"end":254}},"file":"packages/memory/src/policy.ts","span":{"start":249,"end":254},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:7c431c050b2519ebce9622cad4e4ca776fdf40ae0e24f27effc430ebd64bf7ab","meta":{"text":"Resolve a profile by name from the trusted-base policy. Returns `undefined` when the name is absent\n— the CLI layer refuses evaluation absent a TTY approval (PRD line 274: \"Locally refuse profiles\nabsent from the trusted-base policy unless the user explicitly approves them in a TTY\"). CI never\napproves (PRD line 275): a missing profile in the merge-base policy is a hard check failure."}}
{"id":"expl:packages/memory/src/policy.ts@L259","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/memory/src/policy.ts","span":{"start":259,"end":259}},"file":"packages/memory/src/policy.ts","span":{"start":259,"end":259},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:950b7452e7a44247284ce3baf79ee641714685de6d2586774bc94a14ed32a322","meta":{"text":"The effective trusted ref for a policy (explicit or the default)."}}
{"id":"expl:packages/memory/src/policy.ts@L35","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/memory/src/policy.ts","span":{"start":35,"end":35}},"file":"packages/memory/src/policy.ts","span":{"start":35,"end":35},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:b96db5013abf9b7aec0ac4eb1b1d5d64293e9d89f6da5854c046c47d7351861b","meta":{"text":"Stable canonical JSON for hashing (key-sorted)."}}
{"id":"expl:packages/memory/src/policy.ts@L42","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/memory/src/policy.ts","span":{"start":42,"end":51}},"file":"packages/memory/src/policy.ts","span":{"start":42,"end":51},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:bf1c45c5c8c46e15a9e6f1c02897649544e9230e23c9b3d8b60bab3335c40a87","meta":{"text":"One named, bounded assertion evaluated against the gate's captured output. The raw output is NEVER\npersisted (PRD: \"Command output is never persisted verbatim\"); only the assertion's `passed`\nboolean lands on the {@link GateReceipt}. An `execution-assertion` evidence item references a\nreceipt id + assertion NAME — the named result is the admissible signal, not the output text.\n- `exit-code`        — passed iff the command's exit code is in `codes`.\n- `output-contains`  — passed iff the concatenated stdout+stderr contains `needle`.\n- `output-matches`   — passed iff `pattern` (regex, anchored by the caller) matches the output."}}
{"id":"expl:packages/memory/src/policy.ts@L67","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/memory/src/policy.ts","span":{"start":67,"end":71}},"file":"packages/memory/src/policy.ts","span":{"start":67,"end":71},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:e013a9144e8f48ed4f958e361d841c49c24a167a3e217f5b5932e3545096d985","meta":{"text":"A fixed-argument runner profile (PRD line 267). `executable` is resolved + recorded on the receipt\n(no PATH ambiguity at revalidation time). `args` is frozen — a candidate never adds to it. Only\n`permittedEnv` names pass through to the child; every other env var is dropped (least privilege)."}}
{"id":"expl:packages/memory/src/policy.ts@L89","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/memory/src/policy.ts","span":{"start":89,"end":93}},"file":"packages/memory/src/policy.ts","span":{"start":89,"end":93},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:d03e651aac35d6d6875cd35e0d7f6559229b402f4122cdcfb7f6feb5d4614865","meta":{"text":"The trusted-base policy. `trustedRef` is the Git ref whose tree is the source of team trust (PRD\nline 279: \"exact record and decision blobs being present in a configured trusted Git ref\"; default\n`refs/remotes/origin/HEAD`). Without it, committed memories remain `pending` rather than trusted."}}
